# Line endings are normalised to LF on checkout, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. Memfiles and the compiled book are
# byte-exact by specification: `serialize(parse(x))` must reproduce `x`
# exactly, and the round-trip invariant compares bytes. A CRLF checkout
# breaks that guarantee on real user files, not merely in tests — which is
# precisely how it was found, once a dependency bump let Windows CI get far
# enough to run the suite.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stated explicitly for the files the guarantee is actually about, so the
# reason survives someone later relaxing the blanket rule above.
*.mem.md text eol=lf
MEMBOOK.md text eol=lf

# Binary, never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.db binary
